  "text": "## v. Language (pages 50-51)\n[E1] Center press the joystick with the language option selected to explore the options.\n[E2] The following options are available in the menu.\n[E3] English\n[E4] Italian\n[E5] Spanish\n[E6] Portuguese\n[E7] German\n[E8] French\n[E9] The options can be navigated by joystick up and down press and selected by joystick center press.\n[E10] 0\n[E11] 0\n[E12] Press the home button on the LH switch cube to go back.\n\n## 1. APPEARANCE (pages 39-41)\n[E13] From the settings menu center press the joystick with the appearance selected to explore the options.\n[E14] The following options will appear on the screen.\n[E15] Golden line\n[E16] Background\n[E17] Brightness\n[E18] Screen type\n[E19] The options shall be navigated by joystick up & down press and selected by joystick center press.\n[E20] 0\n[E21] 0\n[E22] Press the home button on the LH switch cube to go back.\n[E23] Golden line\n[E24] Center press the joystick with the golden line option selected will open the details to show adjacent to the golden line on the TFT screen.\n[E25] The following options will be shown on the display.\n[E26] ODO\n[E27] Trip 1\n[E28] Trip 2\n[E29] Outside temperature\n[E30] The options shall be navigated by the use of joystick up & down press and selected by the use of joystick center press.\n[E31] Press the home button on the LH switch cube to go back.\n[E32] 0\n\n## 5. INFORMATION (pages 51-53)\n[E33] From the settings menu center press the joystick with the information option selected to explore the options.\n[E34] The following options are available in the system menu.\n[E35] Notification\n[E36] Firmware version\n[E37] The options can be navigated by joystick up and down press and selected by joystick center press.\n[E38] 0\n[E39] 0\n[E40] Press the home button on the LH switch cube to go back.\n[E41] Notification\n[E42] Center press the joystick with the notification option selected to explore the options.\n[E43] The following options are available in the menu.\n[E44] Messages\n[E45] Incoming call\n[E46] Weather alerts\n[E47] Contextual alert\n[E48] Vehicle check alert\n[E49] The options can be navigated by joystick up and down press and selected by joystick center press.\n[E50] Press the home button on the LH switch cube to go back.\n[E51] 0\n\n## IF PRESS JOYSTICK LEFT (pages 36-37)\n[E52] The following details are displayed on the advanced dashboard.\n[E53] Trip 1\n[E54] Trip 2\n[E55] Fuel range\n[E56] Instantaneous fuel consumption\n[E57] Battery gauge\n[E58] Service Due In\n[E59] Engine temperature\n[E60] The above details can be customized in my vehicle option available in the settings menu.\n\n## ELECTRICALS (page 19)\n[E61] Alternator output: 280 W @ 1400 rpm\n    Generation: Alternator, III Phase\n    System: 12 V - DC\n    Battery: 12 V - 8 Ah VRLA\n    Head lamp: 12 V, FPL 1.5 W LED, low beam 12.12 W, high beam + low beam 14.22 W\n    Brake lamp: 12 V, 1.4 W\n    Tail lamp: ............................. 12 V, 0.31 W\n    License plate illuminator: 12 V - LED\n    Instrument cluster: Colour TFT (Thin Film Transistor)\n[E62] Turn signal .......................... Front - 12 V, 2 W x 1 no\n[E63] Rear - 12 V, 4.2 W x 1 no\n[E64] Hazard warning .................. Front - 12 V, 2 W x 2 nos\n[E65] Rear - 12 V, 4.2 W x 2 nos\n[E66] Horn.................................... 12 V, 2.5 A\n[E67] Starter motor...................... 12 V - 0.7 kW\n[E68] Charger port. ....................... USB 2.0 Type C - 5 V, 2 A output\n[E69] (WARNING) Using bulbs/electrical gadgets other than specified rating will lead to overloading/erratic behavior/premature failure of electrical system.\n[E70] (WARNING) Modifications or fitments which are not approved by Royal Enfield, will seriously affect the performance of the vehicle and will render the warranty void."
